new=[
('sheshbazzar','Sheshbazzar','Leader entrusted with temple vessels','Called prince of Judah and later governor.','1:8–11; 5:14–16','The narrative credits him with an early foundation. His identity with Zerubbabel remains uncertain.'),
('mithredath-treasurer','Mithredath, Cyrus’s treasurer','Official counting the temple vessels','Works under Cyrus when the vessels are delivered to Sheshbazzar.','1:8','He is not automatically the letter writer with the same name in chapter 4.'),
('jeshua-priest','Jeshua, son of Jozadak','Priestly leader in the returning community','Works with Zerubbabel. His descendants appear in the marriage investigation.','2:2; 3:2,8; 4:3; 5:2; 10:18','He is distinct from Jeshua ancestors and Levites in service lists.'),
('returning-families','The returning families and temple workers','Community recorded in the return register','The register includes families, priests, Levites, singers, gatekeepers, and other temple workers.','2','The selected group profile does not establish individual identities for every register name.'),
('darius-ezra','Darius, the Persian king','Ruler during temple rebuilding and dedication','Receives the provincial inquiry and authorizes continued work.','4:24; 5; 6','The text connects his reign with restored work. The guide does not invent an exact event-year map.'),
('ahasuerus-ezra','Ahasuerus, the ruler named in opposition','Persian ruler recalled in an accusation notice','Named in a short notice before Artaxerxes’s correspondence.','4:6','The notice is brief. It does not narrate Esther’s complete royal setting.'),
('artaxerxes-ezra','Artaxerxes, the Persian king','Ruler in correspondence and Ezra’s commission','Named in the rebuilding letters and Ezra’s travel authorization.','4; 6:14; 7; 8:1','Chronology and regnal identification require comparison. The chapter sequence is not a dated itinerary.'),
('mithredath-writer','Mithredath, the letter writer','Participant in correspondence against Jerusalem','Named with Bishlam and Tabeel in the Artaxerxes notice.','4:7','Shared spelling does not establish identity with Cyrus’s treasurer.'),
('rehum-chancellor','Rehum, the chancellor','Official opposing Jerusalem’s rebuilding','Writes with Shimshai and other associates.','4:8–23','He is distinct from the Rehum named among returning leaders in 2:2.'),
('shimshai','Shimshai, the scribe','Official composing opposition correspondence','Associated with Rehum in the letter and response.','4:8–23','The account emphasizes written accusations and royal enforcement, not a complete personal biography.'),
('haggai','Haggai','Prophet encouraging temple rebuilding','Works alongside Zechariah during Zerubbabel and Jeshua’s leadership.','5:1; 6:14','Ezra names his encouragement. His separate prophetic book supplies additional material.'),
('zechariah-prophet','Zechariah, the prophet associated with Iddo','Prophet encouraging temple rebuilding','Called son of Iddo in Ezra.','5:1; 6:14','He is distinct from service-list Zechariahs and the earlier prophet killed under Joash.'),
('tattenai','Tattenai','Provincial governor investigating temple work','Governor beyond the River, acting with Shethar Bozenai.','5; 6','He reports the builders’ explanation and seeks documentary confirmation.'),
('shethar-bozenai','Shethar Bozenai','Official participating in the provincial inquiry','Associated with Tattenai and their companions.','5; 6','The narrative records official inquiry and later compliance with Darius’s order.'),
('ezra','Ezra','Priestly scribe studying and teaching Torah','Introduced through a priestly genealogy and supported by Artaxerxes’s commission.','7–10','His leadership joins scripture, administration, prayer, and contested marriage boundaries.'),
('iddo-casiphia','Iddo, the leader at Casiphia','Leader asked to supply temple workers','Ezra sends a delegation to him at Casiphia.','8:17','He is not automatically Zechariah’s ancestor Iddo. Casiphia’s exact location remains uncertain.'),
('sherebiah','Sherebiah','Levite recruited for temple service','Named with his sons and brothers in the traveling community.','8:18,24','Service and treasure stewardship belong together. Verse 24’s priestly wording requires careful comparison.'),
('hashabiah','Hashabiah, the recruited Levite','Temple worker and treasure steward','Named with Jeshaiah and the descendants of Merari.','8:19,24','His name does not identify him with earlier Chronicles officers.'),
('meremoth','Meremoth, son of Uriah','Priest receiving the weighed temple treasures','Works with Eleazar and two Levites at arrival.','8:33','The count records accountability. The brief notice does not provide a full life history.'),
('eleazar-phinehas','Eleazar, son of Phinehas','Temple worker receiving the treasures','Works with Meremoth at the arrival accounting.','8:33','He is not Aaron’s earlier son Eleazar merely because their names match.'),
('jozabad-ezra','Jozabad, son of Jeshua','Levite receiving the weighed treasures','Works with Noadiah, Meremoth, and Eleazar.','8:33','The guide does not automatically merge him with Jozabad in the chapter 10 register.'),
('noadiah-ezra','Noadiah, son of Binnui','Levite receiving the weighed treasures','Named with Jozabad in the arrival accounting.','8:33','He is distinct from the prophetess Noadiah named in Nehemiah.'),
('shecaniah-jehiel','Shecaniah, son of Jehiel','Speaker proposing separation from foreign spouses','Of the descendants of Elam.','10:2–4','His proposal addresses a community boundary. The wives’ own voices and future circumstances are not reported.'),
('jehohanan-eliashib','Jehohanan, son of Eliashib','Person associated with Ezra’s fasting room','Ezra enters his chamber after the proposal.','10:6','This notice does not identify him with every later Jehohanan or Eliashib.'),
('foreign-wives-children','The foreign wives and their children','Households affected by the separation proposal','The account discusses them but does not supply individual portraits or complete personal histories.','9–10','Their beliefs and later lives remain unstated. Interpretive artwork cannot supply missing testimony.'),
('marriage-objectors','Jonathan and Jahzeiah','Named participants opposing the proposal in this translation','Jonathan son of Asahel and Jahzeiah son of Tikvah appear in 10:15.','10:15','Translations differ in this difficult notice. Meshullam and Shabbethai are named as helpers, with the reference requiring care.'),
('shabbethai','Shabbethai, the Levite','Participant named in the contested investigation notice','Named with Meshullam in relation to Jonathan and Jahzeiah.','10:15','The verse’s wording and the direction of support require comparison across translations.')]
